stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> queued : webhook verified or on-demand request accepted

    queued --> running : orchestrator picks the job up
    queued --> cancelled : PR closed or newer commit supersedes it

    state running {
        direction LR
        [*] --> fanning_out
        fanning_out --> collecting : all enabled agents called
        collecting --> aggregating : every agent answered or timed out
        aggregating --> ranking : duplicates collapsed
        ranking --> contextualising : severity order applied
        contextualising --> [*] : similar past issues attached
    }

    running --> completed : every agent returned
    running --> partial : at least one agent timed out or failed
    running --> failed : no agent returned, or persistence failed
    running --> cancelled : superseded while in flight

    completed --> reported : Check Run posted, suggestions published
    partial --> reported : Check Run posted, missing agents marked no result

    reported --> [*]
    failed --> [*]
    cancelled --> [*]

    note right of partial
        partial is a success state, not an error.
        A single slow agent must not block the
        whole review (FR-ORC-02, NFR-04, AC-12).
    end note

    note right of reported
        Suggestions sit in state proposed until the
        developer accepts or rejects them (UC-3).
        Nothing reaches the branch on its own.
    end note
